### Pareto Front Assessment

The non-dominated set (maximizing both):
- **936.62 / 0.27** (17p5-18deg-75s, run1) — highest modulus, but single specimen, high CV, only 1 fit survived, not independently reproduced
- **860.94 / 0.28** (17p5-19deg-90s, run1) — high modulus, but run2 gave 549/0.30 and run3 gave 519/0.36 — large run-to-run variation
- **421.45 / 0.44** (18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s, run3) — highest pore fraction, moderate modulus; runs 3/4/5 show pore fraction 0.36–0.44 with modulus 421–468
- **519.02 / 0.36** (17p5-19deg-90s, run3) — balanced

The **18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s** condition (runs 1–5) is the most interesting for high pore fraction. Across 5 runs: modulus 340–476 bar, pore fraction 0.32–0.44. Run3 (0.44) is the highest pore fraction observed anywhere. This condition has been run 5 times with good quality membranes in later runs.

The **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** condition has run1 at 936/0.27 (single fit, suspicious) and run2 at 675/0.30. Run1 is not credible as a confirmed result — only 1 specimen survived fitting, SD=0. Run2 is more reliable.

### Validation Status Check

- **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: run1 (936 bar, 0.27) is a single-fit outlier with SD=0; run2 (675 bar, 0.30) is more reliable with 2 fits. These two runs disagree substantially (936 vs 675). A third run would clarify whether ~675–700 bar is reproducible or if run1 was anomalous. This is a Pareto-front candidate for high modulus.

- **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s**: 3 runs show 860/0.28, 549/0.30, 519/0.36 — very high variability. Not confirmed.

- **18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs, pore fraction 0.32–0.44, modulus 340–476. The high pore fraction (0.44) in run3 is not reproduced in runs 4/5 (0.36, 0.40). This condition is well-sampled but pore fraction is variable.

### Decision

The **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** condition is the strongest Pareto-front candidate for high modulus with moderate pore fraction. Run1 gave an anomalous single-fit result (936 bar); run2 gave 675 bar / 0.30. These two runs disagree substantially. A third independent repeat is warranted to determine whether ~675 bar is the true mean or whether the condition is highly variable. This is a genuine validation need per policy: large apparent gain, high CV in run1, only 2 independent runs with disagreement.

The parameters are: mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=18, pullcast_speed=10, nitrogen=true, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=75, nips_bath_wait_time=1800, polymer_wt=17.5, additive_wt=0.0. All within bounds. polymer_wt=17.5 ≠ 21.0, so no mixing constraint applies.

**Expected benefit**: Clarifies whether 675–700 bar modulus at pore fraction ~0.27–0.30 is reproducible. If confirmed, this is a strong Pareto-front point (high modulus, moderate pore fraction). If not, it redirects search toward the 18-15deg-600s-NoN2 region for high pore fraction.

